{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "044H", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-quotient-sheaves}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:01a42345a876550b5279b41782bbd410b55e7e8ebf1fa193de25822278e67ba1", "source_text": "Quotient sheaves", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5cc2856ea31178408a73406177a65d43881b1a4f28ad2c5a351f74ebce7640c8", "unit_id": "tag:044H:title"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "044H", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$B$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$j : R \\to U \\times_B U$", "MATH_0005": "$B$", "MATH_0006": "$S'$", "MATH_0007": "$S$", "MATH_0008": "$\\sim_{S'}$", "MATH_0009": "$j(S') : R(S') \\to U(S') \\times U(S')$", "MATH_0010": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-quotient-presheaf}\n\\begin{matrix}\n(\\Sch/S)^{opp}_{fppf} &\n\\longrightarrow &\n\\textit{Sets}, \\\\\nS' &\n\\longmapsto  &\nU(S')/\\sim_{S'}\n\\end{matrix}\n\\end{equation}", "MATH_0011": "$j$", "MATH_0012": "$B$", "MATH_0013": "$U \\times_B U$", "MATH_0014": "$B$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-quotient-presheaf}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6fa55e907014a8f91651edd3d038fb7eed35f84ebd4aa643d15f3a36f43c8f44", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:30d6b3eb8e937dbd73f6d3fdd12babd29aeebfec9c6ffadf8314f1281820d986", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme, and let <MATH_0002> be an algebraic space over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a pre-relation over <MATH_0005>.\nFor each scheme <MATH_0006> over <MATH_0007> we can take the equivalence relation\n<MATH_0008> generated by the image of <MATH_0009>.\nHence we get a presheaf\n<MATH_0010>\nNote that since <MATH_0011> is a morphism of algebraic spaces over <MATH_0012>\nand into <MATH_0013> there is a canonical transformation of\npresheaves from the presheaf (<REF_0001>) to <MATH_0014>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8d0bbfe4931e9192797a942646a451eca0a3aa5bf3425fd97f49a6037b7feacd", "unit_id": "tag:044H:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "044H", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$B \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$j : R \\to U \\times_B U$", "MATH_0003": "$U/R$", "MATH_0004": "$j$", "MATH_0005": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0006": "$j : R \\to U \\times_B U$", "MATH_0007": "$G$", "MATH_0008": "$B$", "MATH_0009": "$U$", "MATH_0010": "$U/G$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{equation-quotient-presheaf}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-groupoid-from-action}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-quotient-sheaf}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3adfd3cb85b927653110ac92f80a5bdf76418cb1c8d6ce34dd648e6449eb7744", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:674b1a580be82ba8e56d2cd3e2540eb0a91f9da9a25ef293d783c4ebba5e060d", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> and the pre-relation <MATH_0002> be as above.\nIn this setting the <TEXTITOPEN_0001>quotient sheaf <MATH_0003><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> associated\nto <MATH_0004> is the sheafification of the presheaf\n(<REF_0001>) on <MATH_0005>.\nIf <MATH_0006> comes from the action of a\ngroup algebraic space <MATH_0007> over <MATH_0008> on <MATH_0009> as in\nLemma <REF_0002>\nthen we denote the quotient sheaf <MATH_0010>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:26223ec46172f2383b2d0d25c251c74dfb78c124528c444f7f745141dd78db6d", "unit_id": "tag:044J:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "044H", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\nR \\ar@<1ex>[r] \\ar@<-1ex>[r] &\nU \\ar[r] &\nU/R\n}\n$$", "MATH_0002": "$(\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0003": "$U/R \\to B$", "MATH_0004": "$j$", "MATH_0005": "$B$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\times_B U$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2d1454115c2cc580a54c0fbaf55982a9c1a070ae64207e051dbcbdc9e992733f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1e31ed93e9e5a30bc4419bfc6bb44884475430af1628b0610cfbee97d63e558d", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis means exactly that the diagram\n<MATH_0001>\nis a coequalizer diagram in the category of sheaves of sets\non <MATH_0002>. Again there is a canonical map\nof sheaves <MATH_0003> as <MATH_0004> is a morphism of algebraic spaces over\n<MATH_0005> into <MATH_0006>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:206b205ff0285b34165bfb54c7a5918bcd01e0620c81f37b50cc2d3083dd74f1", "unit_id": "tag:044H:prose-0002"}
